# Project Guardrails

- Read `AGENTS.md` and the linked planning documents before making non-trivial changes.
- Do not write application code until the user explicitly authorizes implementation.
- Keep exactly two demo profiles, three fixed goals, one local catalog, and no runtime browsing or arbitrary AI actions.
- Never alter the documented nutrition formulas, evidence gate, trend bands, or bounded adjustment rules without explicit approval and a documentation update.
- Keep calculations, catalog validation, weight trends, idempotency, and Draft-to-Active transitions deterministic.
- Never mutate an Active Plan without explicit approval of the currently displayed valid proposal.
- Preserve one action per chat turn; reject malformed model output before it affects state.
- Update the verification plan and evidence when a behavioral requirement changes.

